============================================================
EXPERIMENT 2
DEVELOP A PROGRAM TO ILLUSTRATE THE WORKING OF LED
WITH A PUSH BUTTON
============================================================

AIM:
Interface a push button and an RGB LED with ESP32. Pressing the button turns the red LED ON and releasing it turns the LED OFF.

HARDWARE:
- ESP32 DevKit
- ESP32 Trainer Board
- USB Cable
- Jumper Wires
- Computer/Laptop with Arduino IDE

PIN CONNECTIONS:
- Push Button / SW1 -> GPIO 5
- Red LED / C2 -> GPIO 12
- Trainer 3.3V -> ESP32 3.3V
- Trainer GND -> ESP32 GND

SETUP:
1. Connect GPIO5 to SW1.
2. Connect GPIO12 to C2 (Red LED).
3. Connect 3.3V and GND correctly.
4. Select ESP32 Dev Module.
5. Select the correct COM port.
6. Serial Monitor baud = 9600.

CREATE SKETCH:
exp2_push_button.ino

CODE START
const int buttonPin = 5;
const int ledPin = 12;

void setup() {
    pinMode(buttonPin, INPUT_PULLUP);
    pinMode(ledPin, OUTPUT);
    digitalWrite(ledPin, LOW);
    Serial.begin(9600);
}

void loop() {
    int buttonState = digitalRead(buttonPin);

    Serial.print("Button State: ");
    Serial.println(buttonState);

    if (buttonState == LOW) {
        digitalWrite(ledPin, HIGH);
    } else {
        digitalWrite(ledPin, LOW);
    }

    delay(100);
}
CODE END

PROCEDURE:
1. Upload the program.
2. Open Serial Monitor at 9600 baud.
3. Keep button released.
4. Press the push button.
5. Release it.
6. Observe the LED and serial value.

OBSERVATION:
Released -> HIGH -> Serial 1 -> LED OFF
Pressed  -> LOW  -> Serial 0 -> LED ON

EXPECTED:
When pressed:
Button State: 0
LED ON

When released:
Button State: 1
LED OFF

RESULT:
The push button was successfully interfaced with ESP32 and the red LED was controlled using digital input and digital output.


